// demonstrated.marco — the act of doing ONE thing somebody demonstrated.
//
// # What a Press is, and what it is not
//
// A Press is one interaction a person performed with their own hands while Marco watched, asked
// for again by the name they gave it. The name is a REFERENCE to a demonstration Marco has
// saved, not a search string the play invented — and which demonstration it refers to is written
// in the play's binding record, not in the play, because a digest is not something a reader of a
// play should have to read.
//
// Everything that makes it safe happens below this line and none of it is a Marco noun: the
// control is found again in a fresh look at the screen, the person is asked about this press at
// the moment it is about to happen, and whether it worked is decided from what the screen says
// afterwards. The play asks for an interaction. It does not describe how one is found, who
// permits it, or what counts as having worked.
//
// # Why this is not Theater's Activate
//
// Because `Theater's Activate` means "do to this target what pressing it would do", resolved by
// whichever Actor the stage can cast tonight — the accessibility tree today, sight tomorrow. That
// is a different authority: it finds a control BY NAME among whatever is in front, and it is
// right that it does. A demonstrated press may only ever land on the thing somebody pointed at,
// re-found from that demonstration's own evidence, with a person agreeing to each one.
//
// A single sentence that meant one of those two things depending on who was running the file
// would be the worst of both: the play would read the same, and what it did to the computer would
// not. See [[ADR-243-a-door-of-its-own-and-the-order-in-the-file]].
//
// # Ok means verified
//
// `ok` is returned only when the action's demonstrated outcome stood in fresh evidence after the
// press. Everything else is a failure carrying the sentence that says which: the screen was
// wrong, the control could not be found, the person declined, the evidence said something else,
// the deadline passed with nothing to go on, or the run was cancelled. So a play that continues
// inside `when ok?` continues on a verified action and on nothing weaker.

the Demonstrated is an act.

this exports Press.   // press the demonstrated interaction of this name
